{"title":"Regular polytope","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>regular polytope</b> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polytope\" title=\"Polytope\">polytope</a> with all of its sides and angles equal.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Polytopes_in_different_dimensions\">Polytopes in different dimensions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Regular_polytope&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Polytopes in different dimensions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>A two-dimensional regular polytope is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Regular_polygon\" title=\"Regular polygon\">regular polygon</a>.</li>\n<li>A three-dimensional regular polytope is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Platonic_solid\" title=\"Platonic solid\">Platonic solid</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Regular_polytope&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018105045\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.009 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.013 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 10/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 289/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.765      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.765      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:29289:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018105045 and revision id 229383. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\